<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Vladislav II of Serbia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1270–after 1326</span> · Also known as Vladislav II of Syrmia</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Vladislav II was the son of King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stefan-dragutin">Stefan Dragutin</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbia">Serbia</a>, who ruled the northern lands later called the Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syrmia">Syrmia</a>. After Dragutin's death in 1316 his uncle King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stefan-milutin">Stefan Milutin</a> seized most of these lands and imprisoned him; later released, he claimed the Serbian throne in the 1320s but was defeated by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stefan-decanski">Stefan Dečanski</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/vladislav-ii-of-serbia.jpg" alt="Vladislav II of Serbia" width="320" height="353" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: XIV century serbian painter · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Loza_Nemanjica_Decani_d_3_2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
